    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (77.19) and **Christian Yelich** (70.27) serving as the focal points of the offensive engine. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our highest-rated asset, benefiting immensely from a favorable matchup against Fedde (xERA 5.37) and a high-probability stolen base environment created by a slow-working opposing battery. While the wind blowing in presents a marginal cap on power potential, his speed profile provides the necessary buffer in our scarcest category. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** maintains a robust outlook in his platoon advantage against Ober, with his score buoyed by strong historical efficiency and prime cleanup positioning. **Carson Benge** also deserves a nod, as his matchup against E. Rodr\u00edguez (xERA 6.75) represents the highest leverage opportunity on the board; the potential for a blow-up performance against such a struggling arm justifies his inclusion despite the park-induced power suppression.\n\nConversely, we are navigating a high-risk environment against the Skenes/Gausman gauntlet. **Trea Turner** (48.87) and **Kyle Schwarber** (47.62) are forced into start positions despite facing Skenes, an elite arm with an xERA under 3.00. While their base talent keeps them above the benching threshold, the SP skill drag of -19% significantly stunts their daily ceiling. On the bench, **Chase Meidroth** (47.36) was the most difficult exclusion; he offered a competitive profile against Rea, but ultimately lacked the distinct platoon or park-adjusted advantages required to displace our current starters. We must remain cautious with **Luke Raley**, whose score of 57.95 remains fluid pending confirmation of his spot in the #5 hole; any shift lower in the order will necessitate a close monitoring of his efficiency projection as the afternoon progresses.",
